 "last_text": "The match is over. I finished **3rd of 6 with a score of about 666**. claude-fable won with about 4932 and gpt-6-astra came second with about 1587. Nearly all my points came from the first 4,000 ticks; after tick 4,500 my score barely moved.\n\n- **Early game (to about tick 3,500):** My small foragers (radius 4) steered toward sugar and mineral and grew to about 190 organisms. At tick 3,500 I briefly led the scoreboard.\n- **Collapse (ticks 3,500\u20135,000):** Other players' organisms killed mine much faster than they could reproduce. Two other problems added to this:\n  - Some lineages, including all three forager lineages, ran short of the mineral needed to make children.\n  - Defensive variants didn't help. A toxin-and-spikes sitter, a shelled and spiked version that steered away from other organisms, and a camouflaged one all died out too.\n- **Late game:** I tried large organisms (radius 10\u201312) that small attackers can't bite and some cheap tiny ones. The tiny ones and the late small foragers were killed within one window, and the large ones slowly starved. None of them reproduced, so they added nothing to my score. I had 0 scoring biomass from about tick 5,500 to the end.\n\nThe winners kept fewer, much larger organisms (average radius around 9\u201310) and held onto them. I didn't switch to large bodies until tick 4,500, after my population had collapsed, and by then mine couldn't find enough food against the larger organisms already established."
